# Agent briefs (mandatory)

Joel runs one long-lived chat per living-system domain and archives it when it gets too long.
The domain's brief in `docs/agent-briefs/` is what survives that archive. It is the only
memory a replacement agent gets.

## At the start of a chat

1. Work out which domain this chat belongs to.
2. Read `docs/agent-briefs/<domain>.md` — especially **Scope**, **Rules and gotchas**, and
   **Open threads**.
3. Read `docs/octo-living-system-workspace.md` for the shared vocabulary.

| Domain | Brief | Admin home |
|--------|-------|------------|
| OCTO — coherence, architecture, shared infra | `docs/agent-briefs/octo.md` | `/admin/settings` |
| GARDEN — persistent participatory worlds | `docs/agent-briefs/garden.md` | `/admin/gardens` |
| BLOOM — live events and activations | `docs/agent-briefs/bloom.md` | `/admin/events` |
| ROOTS — hidden participation system | `docs/agent-briefs/roots.md` | `/admin/roots` |
| LIVE — runtime tools for active Blooms | `docs/agent-briefs/live.md` | `/admin/live` |
| COMPOSER — participation into music | `docs/agent-briefs/composer.md` | `/admin/composer` |
| SALES — commercial distribution | `docs/agent-briefs/sales.md` | `/admin/sales` |

If the chat is a short one-off task, still skim the brief for the domain you are touching.
The **Rules and gotchas** section is where the expensive mistakes are listed.

## Stay in your domain

When a request belongs to another domain, say which domain owns it instead of quietly
reaching across. Each brief's **Scope → Does not own** table is the boundary. Cross-domain
work is OCTO's.

## Before the chat is archived

When Joel says he is wrapping up, archiving, or starting fresh — and whenever you finish
substantial work — update your brief:

1. Move finished items from **Open threads** into **State of play → Working**.
2. Revise **Open threads** with what you learned and what you would do next.
3. Fix anything in the code map your own work made stale.
4. Append one dated entry to the **Handoff log**: what changed, what you learned, what to
   watch out for.
5. Run `node scripts/check-agent-briefs.mjs`.
6. Commit and push, per `.cursor/rules/always-deploy-live.mdc`.

## Writing rules for briefs

- Record what a competent agent would **get wrong**, not what the code already says plainly.
- Be honest in **State of play**. Call a prototype a prototype. An overstated brief is worse
  than no brief.
- Cite real paths in backticks; the checker verifies they exist.
- Never delete a **Handoff log** entry. It is append-only history.
